ingredients:
  - "2/3 cup whole wheat flour"
  - "2/5 cup oil (absorbed)"
  - "1/4 cup black gram dal"
  - "1/2 cup spinach"
  - "1 tsp red chili powder"
  - "1/4 tsp mango powder"
  - "1/4 tsp coriander powder"
  - "1/4 tsp carom seeds"
  - "1/4 tsp cumin seeds"
  - "1/4 tsp sugar"
  - "1/4 tsp garam masala"
  - "Salt to taste"
instructions:
  - "Soak dal for 2 hours, drain water completely, and grind coarsely."
  - "Steam spinach and grind it."
  - "Add spinach paste to flour and make smooth dough."
  - "Heat 1 tbsp oil, add all spices, and stir for a minute."
  - "Add ground dal, sugar, salt, and stir-fry for 2-3 minutes."
  - "Divide fillings and dough into 8 equal portions."
  - "Roll out each dough portion into a small roti, place one portion of dal filling in the center, bring the edges together, and press firmly."
  - "Roll the stuffed dough into a puri."
  - "Heat oil and deep-fry till golden on both sides."
  - "Serve hot with chutney or yogurt."
